# What does NOT get uploaded to Vercel.
#
# Round 40 (audit P0-3): the deployment used to carry the whole repo — 38 MB of docs, 124 MB of git
# pack history, 6.8 MB of review screenshots and the owner's master originals. None of that is needed
# to build or run the site; the source of truth for the build is `src/`, `public/`, the config files
# and the handful of assets that `src/assets/manifest.ts` imports directly.

# Review / QA artefacts. They are committed on purpose (the owner reads them in the PR), but they are
# not part of the site; serving them from production was the P0 this rule closes.
artifacts/

# Documentation. Not a route, not imported, and 522 files of it.
docs/

# Root markdown: prompts, handoffs, readme variants.
*.md
!README.md

# Local scratch and editor noise.
.git/
.github/
.vercel
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never upload local state.
.env
.env*.local
/data/

# Test harness sources. The `npm test` suite runs in CI, not on the deploy.
tests/

# NOTE: `AKBAR-NAWASUNDA-ASSETS/` must NOT be listed here. `src/assets/manifest.ts` imports those
# webp/jpg files directly, so excluding the folder fails the build with a module-not-found error.
